out/: 114 wavs at 8 kHz — 6 sources, plus one per channel for every condition and code that held lock long enough to place audio.
Each wav is the FULL duration: what the link delivers, with the output
muted wherever the framer was not locked, so the outages are audible in
place rather than edited out.  "muted" is the fraction of the clip lost
that way and "runs" the number of locked stretches stitched together.
segSNR is scored only where the link was up, so it measures fidelity
and the mute column measures continuity -- they fail independently.
A "--" row never held lock long enough to place any audio.
